<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Windsor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">founded <a href="/years/1917">1917</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Windsor</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Windsor is the royal house of the United Kingdom and other Commonwealth realms, founded in 1917 when King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-v">George V</a> changed the name of the royal house from the German Saxe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coburg">Coburg</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gotha">Gotha</a> to Windsor, after Windsor Castle. The change came because of anti-German sentiment during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, which peaked as Gotha bombers began bombing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>. A royal proclamation of 17 July 1917 announced the new name. Five British monarchs have belonged to the house: George V, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-viii">Edward VIII</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-vi">George VI</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-ii">Elizabeth II</a> and Charles III.</p></div>
